SPEC §6, §7, §8. Kubernetes::Comb::SVG facade: new(combs => ..., title, group_label, columns, size, edges, legend, link, theme) and render returning one self-contained SVG string. Root svg with viewBox, role=img, title and desc summary; one style element with CSS custom properties and a prefers-color-scheme dark block; per cell a g.comb.phase-<phase> with data-name/data-phase, title tooltip, hexagon, name (ellipsis when too long), phase text; borrowed = dashed outline + upstream context; disabled muted; path.dep edges with arrowhead over the fills and under the text; legend with counts; link callback wraps the cell in an anchor (relative or http/https only). One escape function for text and one for attributes, used for every CR value. Deterministic output. Tests parse the SVG with a real XML parser (test-only dependency): phases, borrowed, disabled, edges/legend off, link, escaping in text and attribute, determinism, empty input. Depends on Cell and Layout.

2026-10-02 02:22 Decisions (worker): (1) Draw order: one g.comb per cell holds title+hexagon+texts; edges sit in ONE g.deps BEFORE the comb groups. Hexagon fills are the phase colour at low fill-opacity over the panel, so an edge under a cell shows through the fill and stays under every label - SPEC 6 intent (visible, never hiding labels) without splitting a cell. Letter of SPEC 6 ('over the fills') is not met in document order. Edges are also trimmed: start 0.28*size inside the dependent's outline, arrow tip just before the dependency's outline; same-row non-neighbours get a quadratic bow. (2) Text colour never comes from the phase/theme colour (fg/muted vars only), so any theme colour keeps contrast in light and dark. (3) Output is pure ASCII: everything outside ASCII becomes a numeric character reference, XML-illegal chars are dropped - no encoding question for the caller. (4) link: callback gets the Cell; href refused if it has any whitespace/control char, or a scheme other than http(s):// (colon before first / ? #); protocol-relative //host allowed. A dying callback is caught: carp, cell drawn without link. (5) theme: only phase keys; value must be #hex, a bare name, or rgb()/hsl() over [0-9a-zA-Z%., /-]; else default. One value serves light and dark. (6) CSS is scoped under .comb-svg so an inlined SVG does not style the host page. (7) Borrowed line reads 'from <context>' or 'borrowed' without context. (8) Tooltip phase for Unknown: 'phase: Unknown (<original>)'.

